# -*- mode:org; coding:utf-8 -*-
#+TITLE: alfe-plugin-hooks — the alfe.plugin API and the hook points at every stage
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: feature
#+DEPENDS: alfe-plugin-options
#+BRANCH: master

* Context

Sub-issue of =alfe-plugin-model=: a plug-in must be able to "intervene,
modify or complete alfe's behaviour at every stage of the process"
(pjb, 2026-09-21). EPURE needs the stages between argv and process spawn
(launch argv, working directory, the generated =run.scr= / VBScript);
EPUREE needs the plan; a future plug-in may want any of the others.

* Proposal

- API (=alfe.plugin=): =define-plugin=, =define-plugin-hook=,
  =register-plugin=, =run-hook=, the per-run =context= (options, backend,
  session, workdir, version, per-plug-in state), =plugin-option=,
  =plugin-state=, =plugin-error=, small utilities (AutoLISP string literal,
  VBScript quoting is already =vbs-escape=).
- Three hook kinds: *event* (results ignored), *filter* (threads a value),
  *collect* (concatenates lists). Handlers run in plug-in priority order,
  only for active plug-ins whose =applies-to= contains the running backend.
- Catalogue (call sites in =cli.lisp=, =backend-bricscad.lisp=,
  =backend-autocad.lisp=, =file-protocol.lisp=): =:cli-parsed=,
  =:backend-selected=, =:plan=, =:dry-run-report=, =:workdir-prepared=,
  =:run-common-prelude=, =:run-common-epilogue=, =:launcher-lines=,
  =:launcher-script=, =:launch-argv=, =:launch-options=, =:engine-started=,
  =:pre-action=, =:post-action=, =:pre-shutdown=, =:post-shutdown=,
  =:exit-code=, =:error=. Signatures and call sites: spec chapter "Plug-ins".
- VBScript bridge templates (BricsCAD and AutoCAD) gain two slots, after the
  application object exists and before the =(load …)= is sent, for the
  =:launcher-lines= fragments; the SCR emitters gain before/after-load slots.
- =:pre-action= / =:post-action= make alfe evaluate the plan one action at a
  time; *only when an active plug-in registered one of them* — otherwise
  the plan goes to =eval-plan= in one call, exactly as today.
- A CL error in a handler becomes =alfe.error:plugin-error= (exit 4); a
  =cli-usage-error= or =backend-error= signalled by the handler passes
  through unchanged.

* Acceptance criteria

- With no active plug-in every call site returns its input unchanged; the
  existing 716 checks are untouched.
- A fixture plug-in records each hook it sees; a test asserts the
  lifecycle order for the clautolisp backend and for the mock CAD.
- Hook errors, unknown hook names at registration and =applies-to= gating
  are tested.
